Print a shareable link to one port of a sandbox, for example a dev server on 3000.

Anyone with the link can open that port in a browser until it expires (--ttl,
default 1h, at most 24h): the sandbox edge exchanges it for a cookie scoped to
that port's host. Other ports and envd stay private.

  anona-compute preview <id> 3000
  anona-compute preview <id> 3000 --ttl 15m
  anona-compute preview <id> --revoke          end every link (and live-view token) of the sandbox
  anona-compute preview <id> 3000 --public     serve the port to anyone, no link needed
  anona-compute preview <id> 3000 --private    back to links only

Usage:
  anona-compute preview SANDBOX_ID [PORT] [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help           help for preview
      --private        make the port private again
      --public         make the port public instead of printing a link
      --revoke         revoke every preview link and live-view token of the sandbox
      --ttl duration   link lifetime, 1m to 24h (default 1h)

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each API request (0 = none)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr
